{
  "manifestVersion": 1,
  "id": "locker",
  "name": "Locker",
  "description": "Everything, locked up — a personal password manager over the vault on this phone. Logins, cards, secure notes, identities, Wi-Fi and standalone passwords (and nine template types), each an owner-only locker.item. Secrets are sealed under a key K derived from the member's 24 words and held only in the phone core's memory behind the phone's own lock (biometric, passcode fallback); the list is metadata and every secret is revealed per field, per gesture, receipted before its value exists, and concealed after 30 seconds. One-time codes are RFC 6238 codes the core makes from a seed that is never shown. Custom fields may be sealed; a passkey is stored, never revealed, and cannot be made on the phone. Review is metadata only — the compromised flag, http:// addresses and card expiry — and names weak/reused passwords and breach checking as not checked here. Import reads a password-manager CSV or a Locker export and seals it in; export writes every secret to a plaintext file through the system's save sheet after a fresh owner check. Favorites are the vault's canonical star and tags are the vault's own tags, the same words every other app reads. Every write runs through a typed vault command, receipted.",
  "version": "0.3.0",
  "iconKey": "Lock",
  "colorKey": "rose",
