    {
      "name": "edit-item",
      "verb": "edit",
      "kind": "locker_item",
      "inverse": null,
      "sealed": ["password", "otp_seed", "card_number", "cvv", "content"],
      "chat": "direct",
      "command": "locker.edit_item",
      "phrasings": [
        "change my Netflix username",
        "update the URL on my bank login",
        "fix the cardholder name on my Visa"
      ],
      "description": "Replace an item's type fields through locker.edit_item. This REPLACES and does not patch: every field of the item's type that the input leaves out or empty is cleared, so send the whole draft (a sealed secret you keep goes as the placeholder «sealed»). The title, alias and compromised flag are left alone when omitted. A changed password clears the compromised flag. Tags, the star and the archive are not this command's: they are tag.add and flag.set. Refuses trashed items.",
      "confirmation": "none",
      "input": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "REPLACES, does not patch. Every field of the item's type (username, url, password, one-time-code seed, notes, and the rest of its type's columns) is rewritten from this input, and each one the input leaves out or leaves empty is CLEARED: an edit carrying only a password erases the username, address, seed and notes. Send the whole draft; a sealed secret you are keeping goes as the placeholder «sealed». Only the title, the alias (an empty one clears it) and the compromised flag (a changed password clears it) are left alone when omitted. Tags, the star and the archive are the vault's own (`tag.add`, `flag.set`); custom fields, addresses, the passkey and the memo are their own commands. None is touched here.",
